@Anya hey 👋 there! This is your EOW SanDisk post. It took a big dip as it normally does. This stock what I would consider controlled volatility. Institutions mostly hedge funds know the company and its product are essential just like who they are parallel to. Memory is their game and ai, data centers, our future needs more. 

They manipulate inelastic companies such as this. Large moat high barrier of basically 2 monopolizing yhe sector and are not cannibalizing themselves. Bwcause of the extreme iv that funds have synthetically created they can sell csps for outrageous premiums and be forced to exercise picking up shares at extremely low prices and letting them run and selling Cc 30-40% otm 2 weeks. That's why you the big swings. Just wait for a dip bwcause it's inevitable and either enter  CDS which mitigates risk, provides you more control, and suppresses volatility in. Premium variance all the things i think you dislike about options. In the end the price always goes higher support higher resistance. 

It's all linear and positively correlated. Below is my weekly sandip play. Fuck it I'm calling it sandip. End of next week it will near max value and its a quick $600  barring the wheel keeps spinning. MU is but more stable. Now you can't see no one talked to you about in 26. :)

It sucks when your thesis holds, the investment vehicle you use is ideal, the strikes you choose line up perfectly with your DTE and the road to profit was fuckn rocky and you were close to invalidation, where youre no longer investing but instead hoping. 

All that and you set a sell limit like a pussy cause you dont trust yourself or the market and youre busy and dont want to lose profit. Its a combination but it always sucks to leave money on the table when everything else you did set you up for an upper echelon return, whatever you consider that to be.  Profits profit. 
